      "function": "char_link",
      "line": 1420,
      "code": "fr = find_footnote_ref(&doc->footnotes_found, id.data, id.size);\nif (fr && !fr->is_used) {\n\tif(!add_footnote_ref(&doc->footnotes_used, fr))\n\t\tgoto cleanup;\n\tfr->is_used = 1;\n\tfr->num = doc->footnotes_used.count;\n}",
      "note": "During the second pass over the non-footnote text, `char_link()` hashes the first-line reference name `[^  ]`, `find_footnote_ref()` matches that hash against the registered entry in `doc->footnotes_found`, and this block appends the same `fr` to `doc->footnotes_used`. Without that hash-based lookup and used-list insertion, `parse_footnote_list()` would never reparse the 64-byte footnote body that reaches the crash.",
